A '''vendor''' sold antiques at the ''[[Colossus]]'' [[Colossus marketplace|marketplace]] on [[Castilon]]. When [[Torra Doza]], daughter of platform owner [[Captain]] [[Imanuel Doza]], took an interest in an object he was selling at his stall, he attempted to raise the price from five to twenty [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]], causing her to lose interest.<ref name="Secrets and Holograms" /> The vendor was later bowled over when a [[gorg]] [[Neeku Vozo]] attempted to purchase for lunch got loose and caused a commotion.<ref name="Neekus Reward">{{Resistance|Neeku's Reward}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
The vendor first appeared in the ''[[Star Wars Resistance]]'' episode "[[Secrets and Holograms]]," and is voiced by [[Phil LaMarr]].<ref name="Secrets and Holograms" /> When asked if the character was a [[Bothan]], [[Lucasfilm Story Group]] member [[Matt Martin]] agreed the individual resembled a version of [[Bothan/Legends|Bothan]] from [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] but was unable to confirm if the character was intended to be one. Martin referred to the character as "Nothan."<ref name="Matt">{{Twitter|username=missingwords|url=status/1069721644455739393|name=[[Matt Martin]]|date=2018-12-03|quote=His design certainly looks to be based on one version of the EU Bothan species but I wouldn’t concretely say he IS a Bothan until an official source (of which I am not) confirms that. I’ve been calling him a "Nothan".|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/wip/WtKGu}}</ref>

